        "author": "Russ /russimages",
        "date": "2013-04-30",
        "license": "CC-BY-2.0",
        "observed": "Inspected enlarged park-facing exterior: pale grey warm stone,shallow lead-grey central dome above an arched-window drum,four-way cascade of semidomes/lower small domes,large arched wall fields and pencil minarets with multiple projecting balcony rings and dark pointed caps. Central dome stands substantially below the minaret tips. Park,trees,lamps and separate foreground building excluded."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Courtyard_of_Sultan_Ahmed_I_Mosque.jpg",
        "author": "Maksym Kozlenko",
        "date": "2013-01-02",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-4.0",
        "observed": "Inspected enlarged courtyard photograph: open sky court with continuous pointed open arcades on slender columns,small lead-grey domes above each bay,lower closed dark wooden doors/upper lattice fields in the gallery back wall,raised central portal and a freestanding six-sided fountain pavilion with pointed arches and shallow grey dome. Pale limestone paving and warm stone;fine calligraphy/grilles/ornament abstracted rather than invented."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fatihistanbul.jpg",
        "author": "Hunanuk",
        "date": "2022-07-19",
        "license": "CC0-1.0",
        "observed": "Inspected enlarged southwest aerial: six distinct pencil minarets,four around southeast prayer-hall corners and two at northwest court corners;the shorter courtyard minarets carry two balconies. Open rectangular courtyard is northwest of the domed prayer hall,with long domed perimeter arcades. The central dome,four lower semidomes and small corner domes form a stepped roof cascade. Hagia Sophia is a separate building to the northeast. Outer park,walls,other city buildings and current temporary finish excluded."
      }
    ]
